      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I would suggest that the dominant external actor heavily invested in its current naval expansion might be most susceptible to this historic oversight. Their focus often remains resolutely on grand strategic military gains, causing them to minimize the power of transnational economic pressure points. This priority system often blinds them to the slow, grinding political erosion caused by localized dependency, mirroring past imperial overconfidence. They may view the economy purely as a tool of leverage rather than a fragile ecosystem ripe for local strategic maneuvering.",
      "source": "target",
