      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Breaking such deep-seated patterns is exceptionally rare, suggesting the fault lines are deeply structural rather than merely tactical. However, a shift could occur if power transitions prioritize long-term systemic resilience over immediate, aggressive gains. Leaders who successfully navigate this might adopt a strategy emphasizing complex, multi-layered diplomacy and institutionalizing multilateral frameworks over zero-sum contests. This requires a willingness to accept perceived short-term strategic compromise for enduring, though less visible, regional stability.",
